   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I am facing a problem which I cannot solve.<br>I have several callbackHandlers, sending information from the Shiny Application to JavaScript.<br><br>What works well is when JavaScript digests one callbackHandler at a time, something like<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#606\">Shiny</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">addCustomMessageHandler</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;number1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">value1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">// do something</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">});</span></div></code></div><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#606\">Shiny</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">addCustomMessageHandler</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;number2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">value2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">// do something</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">});</span></div></code></div><br><br>But, what does not work is something like this<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#606\">Shiny</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">addCustomMessageHandler</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;number1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">value1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Shiny</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">addCustomMessageHandler</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;number2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">value2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// do something with value1 and value2</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">});</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">});</span></div></code></div><br><br>Here <i>value1</i> is, i.e., data for a diagram, table etc. where <i>value2</i> is the choice of i.e., a radioButton (in my shinyApp) about the, i.e., diagram type (graph, histogram, etc.), color, display on/off or whatever.<br><br>How to write that in JavaScript?<br><br><br></div>"
    ]
   ]
