     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hm not sure if that does the trick...<div>I dont want to display something, but rather get sever user inputs into JavaScript. The sending back from the stuff happening in JavaScript to the App is no problem. Its rather that the JavaScript side cannot handle multiple changes, made to the same Object...</div><div><br></div><div>Isnt there a way to &quot;collect&quot; the changes (made in the App) in JavaScript? Whenever something changes in the App, update the JavaScript that relies on the values coming from the app. Something like observe() in shiny... That works when its only one callbackhandler, but not with &quot;nested&quot; ones...</div><div></div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>Am Montag, 18. April 2016 10:45:31 UTC+2 schrieb Joe Cheng [RStudio]:</div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">It sounds like you should consider a custom output binding or htmlwidget instead?<br><br><a href=\"http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/building-outputs.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/building-outputs.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792393932465000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Z3Ou8n0JZJg97erlaPuFX\">http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/building-outputs.html</a><br><a href=\"http://www.htmlwidgets.org/develop_intro.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.htmlwidgets.org/develop_intro.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792393932465000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2keInnzc-bFuV-HhEB3zU1\">http://www.htmlwidgets.org/develop_intro.html</a><br></blockquote></div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Mon, Apr 18, 2016 at 1:29 AM Bla Blubb &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">oldn...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div></blockquote></div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I am facing a problem which I cannot solve.<br>I have several callbackHandlers, sending information from the Shiny Application to JavaScript.<br><br>What works well is when JavaScript digests one callbackHandler at a time, something like<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#606\">Shiny</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">addCustomMessageHandler</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;number1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">value1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">// do something</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">});</span></div></code></div><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#606\">Shiny</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">addCustomMessageHandler</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;number2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">value2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">// do something</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">});</span></div></code></div><br><br>But, what does not work is something like this<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#606\">Shiny</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">addCustomMessageHandler</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;number1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">value1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Shiny</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">addCustomMessageHandler</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;number2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">value2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// do something with value1 and value2</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">});</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">});</span></div></code></div><br><br>Here <i>value1</i> is, i.e., data for a diagram, table etc. where <i>value2</i> is the choice of i.e., a radioButton (in my shinyApp) about the, i.e., diagram type (graph, histogram, etc.), color, display on/off or whatever.<br><br>How to write that in JavaScript?<br><br><br></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;Shiny - Web Framework for R&quot; group.<br></blockquote></div></blockquote></div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a rel=\"nofollow\">shiny-discus...@googlegroups.com</a>.</blockquote></div></blockquote></div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/shiny-discuss/b1f23373-4d22-4c45-88b1-1814bfa78c8b%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/shiny-discuss/b1f23373-4d22-4c45-88b1-1814bfa78c8b%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792393932465000&amp;usg=AOvVaw03eI3EVge67ehQq6ys0Kd-\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/shiny-discuss/b1f23373-4d22-4c45-88b1-1814bfa78c8b%40googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792393932465000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1RekeUK0G28mu0d1bPJfKX\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n</blockquote></div></blockquote></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;Shiny - Web Framework for R&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">shiny-discus...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br></blockquote></div>"
