     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>Am Montag, 18. April 2016 21:14:39 UTC+2 schrieb Joe Cheng [RStudio]:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I can think of many different ways to approach what you&#39;re talking about--can you elaborate a bit on your actual scenario? What is your app trying to do with this slider data? What is the goal of the JS that runs at the end of this?</div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Mon, Apr 18, 2016 at 2:41 AM Bla Blubb &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">oldn...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hm not sure if that does the trick...<div>I dont want to display something, but rather get sever user inputs into JavaScript. The sending back from the stuff happening in JavaScript to the App is no problem. Its rather that the JavaScript side cannot handle multiple changes, made to the same Object...</div><div><br></div><div>Isnt there a way to &quot;collect&quot; the changes (made in the App) in JavaScript? Whenever something changes in the App, update the JavaScript that relies on the values coming from the app. Something like observe() in shiny... That works when its only one callbackhandler, but not with &quot;nested&quot; ones...</div><div></div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>Am Montag, 18. April 2016 10:45:31 UTC+2 schrieb Joe Cheng [RStudio]:</div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">It sounds like you should consider a custom output binding or htmlwidget instead?<br><br><a href=\"http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/building-outputs.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/building-outputs.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792393932468000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1kbCG-veXWmiEnWBiJ9o6y\">http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/building-outputs.html</a><br><a href=\"http://www.htmlwidgets.org/develop_intro.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.htmlwidgets.org/develop_intro.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792393932468000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2ZvvxibDNidqLJgVAByGXq\">http://www.htmlwidgets.org/develop_intro.html</a><br></blockquote></div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Mon, Apr 18, 2016 at 1:29 AM Bla Blubb &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">oldn...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div></blockquote></div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I am facing a problem which I cannot solve.<br>I have several callbackHandlers, sending information from the Shiny Application to JavaScript.<br><br>What works well is when JavaScript digests one callbackHandler at a time, something like<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#606\">Shiny</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">addCustomMessageHandler</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;number1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">value1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">// do something</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">});</span></div></code></div><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#606\">Shiny</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">addCustomMessageHandler</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;number2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">value2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">// do something</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">});</span></div></code></div><br><br>But, what does not work is something like this<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#606\">Shiny</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">addCustomMessageHandler</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;number1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">value1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Shiny</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">addCustomMessageHandler</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;number2&quot;</spa